{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"**REJECT for landing.** The round 3 gate still treats an ordinary source map as a cell reference based on its public shape.\n\nAt [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1224), a three-entry map with `:type :cell-ref`, `:id`, and any 64-character string for `:seal` passes the structural test. For example, invoking such a map with `:id` should return its stored value, but the routing at [line 1343](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1343) sends it to admission, which calls `cell/get` at [line 2184](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2184). The VM rejects the invalid seal or nonexistent cell instead of performing the map lookup. The seal prevents a capability bypass; it does not establish ordinary map semantics.\n\nGenuine issued references have the tested shape and continue through admission to the common invoker when their cell contains a callable entry. But the claimed distinction between genuine and non-genuine references is not made by the shape check: [the VM issues references as maps](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:316), and authenticity is established separately against the heap and seal.\n\nThe new tests at [cross_lang_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj:161) concretely assert `42n` for the stated literal and local-binding cases, but both examples have four entries and a three-character seal. Neither exercises a format-matching three-entry map. The “runtime-built” case also binds a literal rather than constructing the map through runtime operations.\n\nThe round 3 diff touches only the two stated files. Its hunks leave the accepted globals-lifecycle and kind-of changes, token-packet authentication, arity guard, witness admission, VM files, and `yang/core/call.cljc` unchanged; I found no call-node surgery, foreign `:code` extraction, or wrappers in that diff.\n\nOne landing qualification: locally, `git merge-base d3a35830 8fb525c4` is `7eb7fc9e`, so the reviewed head does not contain the landed master merge. The quoted checks are accepted as reported, but they do not by themselves establish the behavior of the eventual merge result. No dynamic checks were run in this review."}}
